Rāma rises at dawn and bids cross Jāhnavī --- Brothers arm and reach Gaṅgā with Sītā --- Sumantra pleads to follow and serve in forest --- Vows to shun Ayōdhyā and enter fire if refused --- Rāma bids him return to reassure Kaikēyī --- Sends health obeisance to king and mothers --- Bids fetch Bharata and crown him regent --- Takes banyan-milk locks and boards Guha boat --- Sītā prays to Gaṅgā vowing cattle clothes on return --- Sumantra gazes weeping while brothers hunt deer to tree
